## Project Harness for Claude Code

Import and enforce the canonical `## Development-Harness Boundary` from `@AGENTS.md`. Claude Code uses `.harness/` only for repository-development work; product-runtime agents and orchestration remain application-owned and independent.

## Orchestrated-Worker Protocol

Protocol marker: `ORCHESTRATED_WORKER_CONTINUITY_V1`.

Import `@AGENTS.md` and keep this file limited to Claude-specific exceptions. Keep the persistent user-facing orchestrator open. Delegate a fresh non-fork Agent with a self-contained bounded prompt and no inherited implementation transcript. Review the generated `.claude/settings.json` hooks or merge `.harness/claude-hooks.addition.json`, preserving user settings. SubagentStart supplies `claude-agent:<agent_id>` only to the child; it never claims ownership. That child appends `--worker-id claude-agent:<agent_id>` to `claim`, the exact delegated `resume HANDOFF_ID`, and every mutation, including `verify`, `checkpoint` and `handoff`. Never use shared `session_id` or a parent's identity. Without native delivery, choose a unique manual ID per child; automatic hooks cannot infer it, and manual PreCompact invocation needs the same explicit `--worker-id`.

Use `checkpoint --reason worker_yield --summary "Result" --next "Next task" --worker-id CHILD_ID` for normal completion and `--reason needs_input` for a decision. Reserve `handoff` for true transfer. Automatic PreCompact binds and forwards only the matching native `agent_id`, blocks unknown active ownership or persistence failure, and leaves another identified worker unchanged. SessionStart(compact) emits bounded additionalContext without consuming the packet. Adapter behavior is fixture-tested; native host delivery still needs smoke validation. See the [Claude hooks reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#subagentstart).
